  "id": "higher-order-interaction",
  "term": "higher order interaction",
  "definition": "A higher-order interaction is a group interaction involving more than two individuals at the same time, rather than a series of separate pairwise contacts. In network terms, it is represented as the activation of a hyperlink connecting all members of the group at a specific time.",
